---
/**
 * The server error page. Astro renders it when it cannot handle a request itself (for
 * example a page module that fails to load, before any middleware runs), passing the error
 * as `Astro.props.error`; the middleware logs that error once (src/server/middleware/pipeline.ts).
 *
 * Deliberately self-contained: no layout, component or style imports, so it still renders
 * when a shared build chunk is the thing that failed. It never shows the error's detail.
 */
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Something went wrong · The Watchtower</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>Something went wrong</h1>
      <p>This page could not be shown. Please try again in a moment.</p>
      <p>
        <a href="/">Back to the overview</a>
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
